{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared cases for lib/domain/services/notification_scheduler.dart and",
    "webapp/src/domain/notificationScheduler.ts. Both suites load this file and",
    "must agree on every value.",
    "",
    "Why a fixture rather than two hand-written suites: the same arrangement was",
    "tried for the health score and the two implementations drifted anyway, so",
    "test/fixtures/health_cases.json now exists for exactly this reason. A",
    "notification scheduler is worse to let drift, because the dedupe key is the",
    "identity an already-scheduled OS alarm is cancelled by. If the two sides",
    "disagree on a key by one character, the Flutter app quietly accumulates",
    "duplicate alarms it can no longer reach.",
    "",
    "Vitest cannot import from outside webapp/, so this file is duplicated to",
    "webapp/src/domain/__fixtures__/notification_cases.json rather than",
    "symlinked. Duplicated files drift; both suites assert the two copies are",
    "byte-identical. If that assertion fails, copy this file over that one.",
    "",
    "Times are ISO 8601 with an explicit offset, so both languages parse them to",
    "the same instant without either suite doing timezone arithmetic of its own.",
    "Each case's `prefs` is merged over `basePrefs`.",
    "",
    "The epoch-day integers inside the expected dedupe keys (20686, 20711, ...)",
    "are days since 1970-01-01 in local time. They are only readable next to the",
    "date they came from, so: 2026-08-18 is 20683, and each later day counts up."
  ],

  "basePrefs": {
    "enabled": true,
    "categories": ["budget", "bills", "renewals", "goals", "market", "digest"],
    "quietStartMin": 1320,
    "quietEndMin": 480,
    "reminderHour": 9,
    "billsLeadDays": 3,
    "renewalsLeadDays": 14,
    "goalsLeadDays": 30,
    "digestHour": null,
    "cooldownHours": 24,
    "hideAmounts": true
  },

  "routes": { "budget": "/budget", "dashboard": "/dashboard" },

  "stableIds": {
    "_comment": [
      "FNV-1a 32-bit, masked to the positive-int range. Pinned as literals, not",
      "recomputed by the test, because the whole point is that these numbers are",
      "the same on both platforms and the same next year. The empty string and",
      "the non-ASCII key are here to pin the seed and the UTF-8 encoding."
    ],
    "": 18652613,
    "khazana": 761689677,
    "₹ non-ascii ✓": 2035792502,
    "budget:c-food:2026-08:90": 694152160,
    "bill:r1:20684": 225300953,
    "renewal:i1:20700:14": 1762072395,
    "goal:g1:20800": 670814004,
    "digest:2026-08-18": 1976068324
  },

